The fix is committed and queued to land, but the run ran out of time before the land's verdict came back. I've left #570 open; the manager lands the commit after this run, and the next run finishes the issue.

- **Fix (0960e59c):** as Jody decided (option 1), `cross-test/chaos/fault/fault.go:125` now carries an inline `// #nosec G404 -- seeded on purpose: a chaos run replays from its seed; nothing secret is drawn (accepted: jodydadescott, #570)`. There is no `security-exceptions.yaml` entry.
- **Checked:** gosec over the package no longer reports G404 at that line (it counts one `#nosec`). The fault tests pass, so the same seed still gives the same fault schedule.
- **Full local gates:** they did not all pass (`OVERALL fail=1`). Fifteen gates pass; `current-generation` fails on four `TestDurableSpool*` tests in the generated Go accounting-sink fixture. That failure is already tracked as #341 and is unrelated to this one-comment change. If the land's gates fail on it too, this issue waits on #341.
- **Release:** main has 33 commits since v2.6.1 and v2.6.2 already exists on `release/2.6`, so I tagged nothing on main. The backport pull requests are open, one per release line, each naming the patch tag to cut once it merges: #682 to #688 (`release/2.0` to `release/2.6`, tags v2.0.31 to v2.6.12). The fault tests and gosec pass on each branch; I did not run the full gates on them.
- **Trace check:** no handler was touched. `looper-trace check` reports 8 findings, all in `cross-test/server-runtime/client/go/main.go` and already tracked as #311.
- **Also seen:** gosec reports a low-confidence G101 ("potential hardcoded credentials") at `fault.go:35`, on the string `"token_expiry"`. The scan lowers low-confidence findings, so it doesn't fail the build, and I left it alone.

I posted this progress on the issue and checkpointed the branch. The next run needs to read the land's verdict, update the pull request descriptions with main's commit hash, post the outcome comment and close the issue.
